{
 "elemod": 2,
 "id": "digimono",
 "version": "0.21",
 "title": "Digi Mono",
 "description": "Synth machines for the audio tracks, after the Monomachine's GND and SWAVE machines: MONO SIN, MONO NOISE, MONO SAW (unison, two sub-oscillators), MONO PULSE (PWM, unison, sub), MONO ENS (four oscillators at set intervals, chorus), MONO VO (a formant voice: vowel to vowel, consonants), POLY SIN (three sines at set notes, a pitch envelope) and MACRO (engines ported from Plaits by Emilie Gillet, MIT licence: knob B picks the engine, C/D/E are HARMONICS/TIMBRE/MORPH; Plaits' main output) and CHORDS (four oscillators as a chord: 24 chord types, inversion, spread; sines, or ENS's saw to pulse and chorus), in the FUNC+SRC machine list. They need no sample; the track's filter, amp, LFOs and effects work on them as on a sample. The Monomachine-style machines are a clean-room engine (no Monomachine code or data). The SRC page shows each machine's own knobs (B, C, E, F, G, H); A is TUNE, D the (unused) sample slot. Needs digichain 1.6 or later, which elekloader ticks with it.",
 "category": "Sound",
 "author": "gdeo607",
 "license": "MIT",
 "target": {
  "device": "digitakt-mk1",
  "product": "Digitakt mk1",
  "os": "1.53",
  "syx_sha256": "9bdd44bb6102fb25c143cfab97bc92b7a89c463f795d3112dce89771e29bcc92",
  "section3_sha256": "4b47a9507758ca5669ca02ab2c0374d2c04c98aece445408295cc1dcb265c5df",
